A||||10||fropuff||Fog lamp question||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||07-15-2001||01:47 AM||||Hey guys.  When I get my new front fascia painted, I'm going to put some clear projector fog lamps on as well.  My particular car, an 86 GT, has the factory rear window defrost, which I never use.  I'm wondering if I can use the same switch for my fog lamps.  I'd just disconnect the wires from the switch for the defrost, and wire up the fog lamps.  If I can't, I might just get a new switch unit.  Thanks for any help!  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||07-15-2001||09:49 AM||||Its a great idea - and its stil a 'defogger' is a sense - front view defogger instead of rear window (c:<P>  I would recommned you find the RW defogger relay - and run your fog lamps off that - or wire the car so the switch controls a new relay that powers the lamps - I dont think the dash switches are designed to handle a lot of current - but im pretty sure the RW defogger relay can handle 30 amps.<P>  One of the things Im planning on doing is putting driving lights on the front of my  car and wiring them as daytime running lights or driving lights - MY '85SE is silver and people keep pulling out in front of me - its the same color as dry pavement!<P>  almost nailed a caddy last friday.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fleabitdog||07-15-2001||09:59 AM||||Fropuff, skitime just did his with the r/w defroster. I am not sure of the details but you can email him. I am sure he will tell you in detail how he ran the wires and what he did to tie them into the switch. I beleive he modified the switch in some way for a special feature. Dave||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||07-15-2001||03:18 PM||||I guess it's posible.<P>The switch and/or control modul would need to be altered to do this. The switch is presently only a momentary contact. the control modul is programmed to turn off after so many minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000004||skitime||07-15-2001||06:36 PM||||fropuff - You need to modify several things to make the circuit work. First you have to modify the switch so that the switch stays on. Remove a spring under the rocker.  Second, you must remove the stock relay because it is designed to automatically shut off after ten minutes and install a normal relay in its place. Third, I changed the relays trigger source to the parking lights circuit so that they go on and off only it the parking lights are on.  That way I still have the blue dingy thing to remind me it the driving lights are on.   If you have question email me.<P> <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||07-15-2001||06:56 PM||||i used the switch position but replaced the defog switch with a lited rocker so I can tell there on from inside. also I wired them to ignition hot so they wouldnt work with key off. Took a little more work, but I replaced my headlite/park lite switch with matching ones too. with the glow I can tell at a glance which lights are on.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||07-15-2001||07:03 PM||||forgot i got PIP now. 1st real try. heres my dash with lited rockers on all lites.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1000436_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||skitime||07-15-2001||07:34 PM||||BTW, This rear defroster switch is lighted too and also indicates the lights are on with the bright yellow indicator that is stock.  I want ot figure out how to iluminate the headight switch as well as the window switch.||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||07-15-2001||07:59 PM||||I think the only way your going to get any lite on OEM switch or window switch is drilling a tiny hole near it and put in a miniature 12v lite or LED. I dont remember any late GM with lit lite switch. maybe caddy has lit window switch that might work.||||reg||1
Z||000009||skitime||07-15-2001||08:22 PM||||Roger, thats what I was thinking too.  I know someone on the forum put Grand Prix window switches in to get lights and the autodown feature.||||reg||1
